# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PUPPET MASTER - Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⚠️ Never commit .env to git!
# Values are read as dotenv data, not executed as shell.
# Quote values that contain spaces or angle brackets.
# You do NOT need to hand-prepare this file: the framework bootstraps it.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENV LIFECYCLE — three distinct contracts, not one mixed workspace
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. RUNTIME APP CONFIG — the narrow surface the app reads via process.env
#    and validates in src/lib/server/utils/env.ts. There are NO soft dev
#    fallbacks: a missing required value (TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY when 2FA is
#    enabled) fails clearly and early.
# 2. LONG-LIVED DEPLOY SECRETS — generated ONLY during first-time bootstrap
#    (ensure_framework_env in scripts/lib/deploy-env.sh,
#    scripts/env-bootstrap.mjs). Never read by the app; used only by
#    setup/deploy/rotation. Steady-state `setup`/`deploy` validate them and
#    fail instead of regenerating; restore from a backup if lost.
# 3. FIRST-RUN OPERATOR INPUTS — site facts and deploy transport the operator
#    provides (`npm run setup` prompts on a TTY) or the framework defaults.
#
# Lifecycle behavior:
#   - first run (no setup state file yet, or explicit PM_ENV_INIT=1):
#     `npm run dev`, `npm run db:seed`/`db:reset`, `npm run setup` and
#     `npm run deploy` may create .env from this template and auto-generate
#     the long-lived secrets.
#   - steady state (setup state exists): `setup`/`deploy` validate the
#     initialized .env and FAIL instead of regenerating anything.
#
# Legend:
#   🔒 generated by bootstrap (do not hand-fill; restore from a backup)
#   🚩 operator site fact (asked by `npm run setup`)
#   ⚙️ optional project setting (read only when set)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONTRACT 1 — RUNTIME APP CONFIG
# Validated by src/lib/server/utils/env.ts. The app reads these at runtime;
# missing required values fail clearly and early (no soft dev fallbacks).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite database path (runtime; deploy mounts /app/data over the same file).
DATABASE_URL=./data/sqlite.db

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EMAIL (SMTP) (⚙️ optional — required if features.contactEmailConfirmation)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sends confirmation email to users who submit contact form
#
# Common SMTP providers:
# - Yandex: smtp.yandex.ru:465
# - Gmail: smtp.gmail.com:587 (requires App Password)
# - Mailgun: smtp.mailgun.org:587

SMTP_HOST=smtp.yandex.ru
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=your-email@yandex.ru
SMTP_PASS=your-app-password
SMTP_FROM="Your Site Name <your-email@yandex.ru>"

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2FA SECRET ENCRYPTION (🔒 runtime-required when 2FA enabled; generated by
# bootstrap — keep stable between deploys)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Encrypts 2FA secrets at rest. The server fails fast without it when
# FEATURES.twoFactorAuth is enabled (src/hooks.server.ts). Bootstrap generates
# it on first run; keep the same value between deploys (restore from backup).
# Generate manually if needed: openssl rand -hex 32
TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-64-character-hex-string-from-openssl

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY (⚙️ optional — error tracking, audit I-3 hardening)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave SENTRY_DSN empty to disable error tracking entirely.
# When set, server errors are reported to Sentry (hooks.server.ts wires
# sentryHandle + handleErrorWithSentry only when this is present).
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT defaults to NODE_ENV; SENTRY_RELEASE defaults to
# APP_BUILD_SHA / GIT_COMMIT_SHA.

# SENTRY_DSN=https://public_key@ingest.sentry.io/project_id
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# SENTRY_RELEASE=

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAMAV (⚙️ optional — virus scanning, audit I-2 hardening)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploads are admin-only in the current config; ClamAV scanning is optional
# hardening and FAILS OPEN (uploads proceed when disabled/unavailable).
# Enabled by default in production, disabled in dev. Requires the clamscan
# package + ClamAV daemon on the server.
#
# CLAMAV_ENABLED=true
# CLAMAV_SOCKET=/var/run/clamav/clamd.ctl

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRUST PROXY (⚙️ optional — audit I-7 rate limiting)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to true ONLY when running behind a trusted reverse proxy (e.g. Traefik)
# that strips client-supplied X-Forwarded-For/X-Real-IP headers. When false
# (default), the socket address is used for rate limiting so clients cannot
# spoof their IP to bypass per-IP limits.
#
# PM_TRUST_PROXY=false

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HIBP BREACH CHECK (⚙️ optional — audit N-4 password hardening)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When true, the password change endpoint checks new passwords against the
# HaveIBeenPwned range API (k-anonymity: only a hash prefix is sent). FAILS
# OPEN — an unreachable API never blocks a password change. Default: off.
#
# PM_FEATURES_HIBP=false

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONTRACT 2 — LONG-LIVED DEPLOY SECRETS
# 🔒 Generated ONLY during first-time bootstrap (ensure_framework_env).
# Never read by the app; used by setup/deploy/rotation. Steady-state
# setup/deploy validate these and fail instead of regenerating. Restore from a
# backup if lost — regenerating would orphan encrypted settings / 2FA secrets.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETTINGS ENCRYPTION (🔒 generated by bootstrap — do not hand-fill)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Encrypts sensitive settings (API keys, tokens, passwords) stored in the
# database. Not read by the app at runtime — deploy/rotation only.
#
# ⚠️  Keep this key stable between deploys and back it up: losing it means
#     losing access to all encrypted settings. Restore the old value from a
#     backup when reinstalling.

PM_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-64-character-hex-string-from-openssl
# SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-64-character-hex-string-from-openssl

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADMIN BOOTSTRAP PASSWORD ROTATION (🔒 generated by bootstrap)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three privileged bootstrap passwords are auto-generated on first run —
# do NOT hand-fill them. They are used by the deploy rotation step
# (node scripts/rotate-admin-passwords.mjs --apply) and by enforced seeding;
# rotated/bootstrap accounts are forced to change the password on first login
# before any admin surface is reachable.
#
# To use explicit values instead (e.g. from a password manager), set them here
# and the framework keeps them (only missing/placeholder values are generated).
# Local development: `npm run db:seed` / `npm run db:reset` never fail because
# of the project's static PM_MODE (even 'build'); they use these passwords when
# set, otherwise they generate one-time random credentials and print them.
# Production / enforced seeding fails fast without strong values when
# NODE_ENV=production OR PM_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_ENFORCE=true.
# PM_ADMIN_USER_* maps to the built-in editor/content-user account.
PM_ADMIN_PASSWORD_ROTATION_ENABLED=true
PM_ADMIN_MASTER_EMAIL=master@example.com
PM_ADMIN_MASTER_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-random-password
PM_ADMIN_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
PM_ADMIN_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-random-password
PM_ADMIN_USER_EMAIL=editor@example.com
PM_ADMIN_USER_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-random-password
# Set to true to make `npm run db:seed` / `npm run db:reset` fail fast without
# the credentials above outside of NODE_ENV=production.
# PM_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_ENFORCE=false

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY ACCESS (🔒 generated by bootstrap / setup)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY_USER_PASSWORD: sudo password for the deploy user (generated).
# DEPLOY_SSH_KEY: local private key path used when SSH_KEY=true (generated by
# setup as a keypair). Restore from a backup when reinstalling.
DEPLOY_USER_PASSWORD=
DEPLOY_SSH_KEY=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONTRACT 3 — FIRST-RUN OPERATOR INPUTS
# Site facts (🚩, asked by `npm run setup` on a TTY), deploy transport
# (🚩/defaulted by the framework), and optional project settings (⚙️, read only
# when set). Preflight fails fast listing exactly which site facts are missing.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SITE CONFIGURATION (🚩 site fact — asked by `npm run setup`)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your primary production domain (used for URLs, monitoring, deploy, and
# the canonical HTTPS health check).
SITE_DOMAIN=example.com

# Optional additional domains routed through Traefik and covered by Let's Encrypt.
# These hosts redirect permanently to SITE_DOMAIN. Use bare domains only, not URLs.
# Separate multiple aliases with commas or spaces.
# SITE_DOMAIN_ALIASES=www.example.com

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY BOOTSTRAP (🚩 site facts + framework defaults)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# First-time server setup is driven from .env.
#
# Operator-provided site facts:
# - SERVER_IP: public IP of your new VPS (asked by `npm run setup`)
# - SERVER_ROOT_PASSWORD: temporary root password from your provider — only
#   used for the first password bootstrap / sudo recovery
#
# Framework-defaulted (override only if needed):
# - SSH_KEY / PM_DEPLOY_AUTH_MODE: ssh_key by default; password auth only if
#   you opt into it
# - DEPLOY_USER: default 'deploy'
# - SERVER_SSH_HOST_KEY_FINGERPRINT: optional trusted fingerprint; when blank
#   the scripts trust the first ssh-keyscan result and pin it into known_hosts
#
# If SSH_KEY=false, setup uses SERVER_ROOT_PASSWORD to create/update DEPLOY_USER
# and keeps password SSH enabled for deploys.

SERVER_IP=123.45.67.89
SERVER_ROOT_PASSWORD=the-root-password-from-vps-provider
SERVER_SSH_HOST_KEY_FINGERPRINT=
# PM_DEPLOY_REQUIRE_HOST_FINGERPRINT=true
SSH_KEY=true
DEPLOY_USER=deploy
PM_DEPLOY_AUTH_MODE=ssh_key
# PM_DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS_FILE=./ansible/known_hosts

# Email for Let's Encrypt certificate issuance (🚩 site fact)
ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# Docker-first deploy transport (framework-defaulted).
# Default deploy mode builds the app image on this dev PC, pushes only changed
# layers through an SSH tunnel to a private registry on the server, then the
# server pulls locally from that registry. No third-party registry is required.
# Framework defaults live in framework.versions.json; project .env values override them.
TRAEFIK_IMAGE=traefik:v3.1
PM_DOCKER_DEPLOY_MODE=ssh-registry
PM_DOCKER_REGISTRY=
PM_DOCKER_IMAGE=puppetmaster2-app
PM_DOCKER_USERNAME=
PM_DOCKER_TOKEN=
# Private server registry settings for PM_DOCKER_DEPLOY_MODE=ssh-registry.
# The registry binds to server localhost; deploy reaches it through SSH only.
PM_DOCKER_SSH_REGISTRY_HOST=127.0.0.1
PM_DOCKER_SSH_REGISTRY_PORT=5000
# PM_DOCKER_SSH_REGISTRY_IMAGE=registry:2
# PM_DOCKER_SSH_REGISTRY_LOCAL_PORT=5000
# Emergency full-image stream fallback for PM_DOCKER_DEPLOY_MODE=local.
PM_DOCKER_STREAM_COMPRESSION=zstd
# PM_DOCKER_IMAGE_TAG is optional. By default deploy uses the generated build version.
# PM_DOCKER_IMAGE_TAG=
# PM_APP_CONTAINER_NAME is auto-derived from SITE_DOMAIN in the new Docker Compose system.
# PM_APP_NETWORK is hardcoded as pm-shared (shared across all projects on the VPS).
# These settings are no longer used by the deploy system.
# PM_APP_CONTAINER_NAME=puppetmaster2-app
# PM_APP_NETWORK=puppetmaster2

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY DATABASE PATH + SCHEMA ROLLOUT (framework-defaulted)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production deploys declare the app-visible path as /app/data/sqlite.db,
# and Docker mounts that to /home/<deploy-user>/app/shared/data/... .
PM_DEPLOY_DATABASE_URL=/app/data/sqlite.db

# Optional rollout policy override for schema-breaking releases.
# Default is PM_DEPLOY_SCHEMA_MODE=compatible.
# For breaking schema changes, open a maintenance/read-only window and use:
# PM_DEPLOY_SCHEMA_MODE=maintenance
# PM_DEPLOY_MAINTENANCE_ACK=1
#
# Deploy infrastructure overrides (audit I-16 — documented here so deploy.sh
# preflight validation matches .env.example):
#
# PM_DEPLOY_DATA_VOLUME=pm_data          # Docker volume for the SQLite data dir
# PM_DEPLOY_UPLOADS_VOLUME=pm_uploads    # Docker volume for uploaded files
# PM_DEPLOY_ANSIBLE_RETRIES=3            # Ansible retries on transient failures
# PM_DEPLOY_ANSIBLE_RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS=5
# PM_APP_CONTAINER_NAME=pm-app           # Running container name (used by restore-db.sh)
# PM_APP_NETWORK=pm-shared               # Docker network for the app container
#
# Backup cron (audit I-17 / E-6 — optional automated DB backups):
# When true, Ansible installs a daily (02:00) cron job running
# scripts/backup-db.sh --remote for this project. Enable S3 vars below for
# offsite storage.
# PM_DEPLOY_BACKUP_CRON=false

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROJECT MODE + APPLICATION VERSION (project identity)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PM_MODE controls whether the /init wizard is shown (scripts/init-cli.ts).
# The app's runtime PM_MODE is static in src/project/site-config.ts — this
# .env value is not read by the app.
# Values:
#   unconfigured - Show /init wizard (default for new projects)
#   build        - configured project mode
#   develop      - PM showcase/testing mode
PM_MODE=unconfigured

# Stable app/product version shown in admin and health endpoints.
# This is separate from the build version, which is generated from deploy time.
APP_VERSION=0.1.0

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADMIN MONITORING (⚙️ optional project settings)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional PM-native resource metrics. Netdata is used as a local metrics source;
# the admin panel renders the UI itself and does not expose Netdata publicly.
PM_MONITORING_NETDATA_ENABLED=true
NETDATA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:19999

# Private PM ops agent for admin diagnostics/actions.
# The agent is deployed as an internal-only sidecar with Docker socket access;
# the Nuxt app calls it through the private Docker network using this token.
PM_OPS_AGENT_ENABLED=true
# PM_OPS_AGENT_TOKEN=optional-random-token-defaults-to-PM_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MONITORING (⚙️ optional project settings)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Subdomain for Uptime Kuma monitoring dashboard
# Full URL will be: https://{UPTIME_KUMA_SUBDOMAIN}.{SITE_DOMAIN}
# If configured, admin health page will show a link to this dashboard
# UPTIME_KUMA_SUBDOMAIN=status

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S3 STORAGE (⚙️ optional project settings)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required if: storage.provider = 's3' in puppet-master.config.ts
# Supports AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces, etc.
#
# For Cloudflare R2:
#   S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
#   S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://pub-<id>.r2.dev or your custom domain
#
# For AWS S3:
#   S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.<region>.amazonaws.com
#   S3_REGION=us-east-1
#
# Visibility modes:
#   S3_VISIBILITY=public  -> requires S3_PUBLIC_URL
#   S3_VISIBILITY=private -> objects are served through signed /api/media/s3/* proxy URLs
# Optional:
#   S3_PROXY_SIGNING_KEY overrides S3_SECRET_KEY for proxy URL signatures.

S3_ENDPOINT=https://your-endpoint.com
S3_BUCKET=your-bucket-name
S3_ACCESS_KEY=your-access-key
S3_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key
S3_REGION=auto
S3_VISIBILITY=public
S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://cdn.yoursite.com
# S3_PROXY_SIGNING_KEY=replace-with-long-random-secret

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXTERNAL API DATA SOURCE (⚙️ optional project settings)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required if: dataSource.provider = 'api' or 'hybrid' in puppet-master.config.ts
# Allows using external REST API instead of local SQLite database
#
# Use cases:
# - Headless CMS integration (Strapi, Contentful, Sanity, etc.)
# - Microservices architecture
# - Multi-instance deployments with shared data
# - Cloud-native applications

# API base URL (without trailing slash)
API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1

# OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials (Recommended for production)
# Most secure method - tokens auto-refresh
API_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
API_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
API_TOKEN_URL=https://auth.example.com/oauth/token

# Alternative: Static JWT token (simpler for development/testing)
# Requires manual rotation when expired
# API_JWT_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Alternative: API Key (basic auth - least secure)
# Only use for internal/trusted networks
# API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# Token refresh timing (seconds before expiry)
API_TOKEN_REFRESH_BUFFER=300

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REDIS CACHE (⚙️ optional project settings — multi-instance deployments)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required if: Running multiple app instances behind load balancer
# Enables shared cache across instances for API data
#
# For single-instance deployments, in-memory cache is sufficient

# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# REDIS_PREFIX=pm-cache:
